    {
      "id": "44ad78cdca7ba5d621d895ec2c1a8d48f4142ec7",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 508441751,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "The description of the protocol can be improved I think, it is currently quite vague. Additionally, the \"type\" can be clarified. What about this:\n\n```suggestion:-0+0\nHyperText Transfer Protocol version 2 (HTTP/2) allows multiplexing multiple HTTP requests and responses over a single connection and uses a binary encoding consisting of frames. The HTTP/2 statistics window shows the total number of HTTP/2 frames and also provides a breakdown per frame types such as `HEADERS`, `DATA`, etc.\n\nAs HTTP/2 traffic is typically encrypted with TLS, decryption must be configured in order to see HTTP/2 traffic. See the link:{wireshark-wiki-url}TLS[TLS wiki page] for details.\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 2415432,
            "username": "Lekensteyn",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Peter Wu",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/efcf30db53f30b15e7c905ef37bd4dc44d87573bd92baf97cd707115d3fcd0c0?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/Lekensteyn"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-02-13T18:20:22.697Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-02-13T18:20:22.697Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 87228579,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "commit_id": null,
          "position": {
