          "resolved_at": "2021-02-16T15:24:28.032Z",
          "suggestions": [
            {
              "id": 816060,
              "from_line": 663,
              "to_line": 663,
              "appliable": false,
              "applied": false,
              "from_content": "Hypertext Transfer Protocol version 2 (HTTP/2) is a basic protocol for the application layer which plays a role in the resources connectivity. The HTTP/2 statistics window shows the counter for the captured packets in total and also can be devided by type. You can filter, copy or save the data to a file.\n",
              "to_content": "HyperText Transfer Protocol version 2 (HTTP/2) allows multiplexing multiple HTTP requests and responses over a single connection and uses a binary encoding consisting of frames. The HTTP/2 statistics window shows the total number of HTTP/2 frames and also provides a breakdown per frame types such as `HEADERS`, `DATA`, etc.\n\nAs HTTP/2 traffic is typically encrypted with TLS, decryption must be configured in order to see HTTP/2 traffic. See the link:{wireshark-wiki-url}TLS[TLS wiki page] for details.\n"
            }
          ],
